      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T02:54:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m still not clear on it. What\u0027s combination would cause the failure.\n\nThe goal is to have the same flag value during the prebuild, and cts in nextfood.\nSo how to control the flag for the prebuild? Does it not follow the trunk stable process to enable the flag? or you just say there is a time gap between cts and prebuild for the flag enablement.",
      "parentUuid": "f424641d_2d751f30",
      "revId": "a24423dc7609d6be97de9d5f95ad3633c4ffec18",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d05eb2a_36e30c3a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-06T02:41:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "cts are build from source and are using the last nextfood approved build.  \nBluetooth prebuilt may take more time as we need it to be build / tested / drop.\n\n\u003e So how to control the flag for the prebuild? \n\nYou do not control it directly, you need to ask @girardier@google.com by using the form at go/bt-flag-trunkfood when you want to move to trunkfood (and not nextfood, so it give time to build / test / and prepare the drop)\n\n\u003e Does it not follow the trunk stable process to enable the flag?\n\nPartially, but prebuilt are in the way. I recommend looking at go/bt-ts-workflow\n\n\nI still prefer to have flag failure on nextfood than on all presubmit and hence I am +2 this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "fcb5128d_864159e3",
      "revId": "a24423dc7609d6be97de9d5f95ad3633c4ffec18",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
